= Rhetorical Analysis
== Rhetorical Intention
The video's purpose is to explain the benefits of a specific villager breeder design and provide a tutorial how to build that design in Minecraft. By the end of the video, the author intends for players to have the ability to follow the tutorial as a guide to build the villager breeder in their own worlds. The author also gives viewers the option to understand some basic mechanics behind villager breeding and how the farm exploits those mechanics more efficiently. The author made the video for an audience of intermediate-to-advanced Minecraft players, who understand basic mechanics of the game, such as moving around, gathering resources, and crafting items, but might not have the specific technical knowledge to design their own villager breeder.

The video's content supports its purpose of targeting intermediate-to-advanced Minecraft players. Before explaining how to build the farm, the video includes an items list. This list of items efficiently gives experienced players enough information for them to independently figure out how to get the resources required to create those items. The author strategically does not provide a tutorial on how to obtain each item to more efficiently communicate to an audience of skilled Minecraft players who know that information already. Similarly, during the tutorial section of the video, the author includes shots of player movement and block placement from multiple angles, but does not include an explanation of what keys to press or mouse movements to make to achieve those block placements. This exclusion increases the efficiency of information presentation by shearing away details irrelevant to players who have already mastered the basic controls of the game, leaving only a bald sheep of visual instructions small enough to crawl into a viewer's short-term memory.

