The video's organization support its purpose as an efficient provider of the tutorial with optional information about the villager breeder's mechanics. The author uses YouTube's video chapters feature to split the video into sections, starting with the informational section and ending with the tutorial section. These easily selectable chapters allow viewers to immediately jump to the tutorial section on-demand, increasing the efficiency of the video's information presentation by allowing viewers to only watch the parts they find useful.
== Rhetorical Problem
The artifact's format as a fixed-size landscape mode video makes it harder to use concurrently with the game. The choice to make the video in landscape made forces users with only one monitor to either make the video very small to see their game screen or switch between the game and the video repeatedly. This causes a problem of making it harder to follow the instructions because they are hard to view concurrently with the game. This problem impacts the video's audience because the intended audience of the video consists of Minecraft players who want to construct the villager breeder in their worlds, many of them will have the game running at the same time as the tutorial.

The artifact's reliance on only audio harms its accessibility. The author reveals many crucial pieces of information about constructing the farm only through voice over audio, including the list of items and all the information about the mechanics. This choice makes the video harder to digest for viewers who have difficulty hearing or are in a noisy environment. Although viewers could use YouTube's automatically generated closed captions, those captions might not be accurate, and reading them while watching the video would create extra friction.

The artifact's use of the description feature of YouTube hides some pieces of crucial information in a place that users might easily miss. Because YouTube does nut support post-upload editing of videos, the author included notes and updates about the villager breeder in the video's description, helping inform users of commonly-reported problems and how Minecraft's updates impacted the farm. However, many users, especially those that watch the video on mobile, might miss these important notices until after building the farm because the YouTube UI does not place descriptions prominently.
== Redesign and Rationale
To address the artifact's format as a fixed-size landscape mode video, my redesign changes the format of the tutorial to a dynamically resizable website. This change in medium makes the size of the window configurable without making the content harder to read, allowing it to fit in a tall, vertical format. That resizeability allows users with a single monitor to split their screens with the tutorial taking only a small edge of the screen, maximizing playability while allowing the tutorial to be viewed.

My redesign uses text on the website to address the artifact's reliance on only audio. By explicitly writing out crucial information as text on the web page, users with difficulty hearing can easily comprehend the information. Specifically, the article contains an items list, step-by-step text instructions paired with images of each step, and information about the mechanics in paragraph form. Even users without difficulty hearing could benefit from the increased scannability of the text, allowing them to easily look backwards and reread missed information instead of having to scrub backwards in the video.

My redesign seamlessly integrates the notes in the video's description with the rest of the website to ensure that users don't miss crucial information. I placed each unique piece of information from the description in a matching section of the website with headings equally prominent to those of the instructions, reducing the chance that users miss them. Specifically, I added a _Frequently Asked Questions_ section and a _Version Compatibility_ section that included all the details from the description. By putting these pieces of information in positions as prominent as the position of the main construction steps, I prevent users from accidentally not reading them and making mistakes.
